{"type":"standard","title":"Joe Lombardo","displaytitle":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Joe Lombardo</span></span>","namespace":{"id":0,"text":""},"wikibase_item":"Q28033703","titles":{"canonical":"Joe_Lombardo","normalized":"Joe Lombardo","display":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Joe Lombardo</span></span>"},"pageid":8692187,"thumbnail":{"source":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d1/Joe_Lombardo_%2855512849370%29%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Joe_Lombardo_%2855512849370%29%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","width":330,"height":441},"originalimage":{"source":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/d/d1/Joe_Lombardo_%2855512849370%29%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","width":1686,"height":2255},"lang":"en","dir":"ltr","revision":"1374183013","tid":"b941da7d-acfd-11f1-9bc0-8975ff6f84bc","timestamp":"2026-09-10T09:55:16Z","description":"Governor of Nevada since 2023","description_source":"local","content_urls":{"desktop":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Joe_Lombardo","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Joe_Lombardo?action=history","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Joe_Lombardo?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Joe_Lombardo"},"mobile":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Joe_Lombardo","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:History/Joe_Lombardo","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Joe_Lombardo?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Joe_Lombardo"}},"extract":"Joseph Michael Lombardo is an American politician and former law enforcement officer serving since 2023 as the 31st governor of Nevada. From 2015 to 2023, he was the 17th sheriff of Clark County, capping a 34-year career in law enforcement. Lombardo is a member of the Republican Party.","extract_html":"<p><b>Joseph Michael Lombardo</b> is an American politician and former law enforcement officer serving since 2023 as the 31st governor of Nevada. From 2015 to 2023, he was the 17th sheriff of Clark County, capping a 34-year career in law enforcement. Lombardo is a member of the Republican Party.</p>"}